    "retarget_pose_policy": "Three retarget poses were built per skeleton: reference pose, limbs auto-aligned to Manny, and all bones auto-aligned. All-bones alignment minimizes segment-direction mismatch versus Manny (0.3 to 1.6 degrees) but pitched every legacy face down, because those head and spine bones tilt differently from Manny while the faces already look forward. Limbs-only alignment is the policy: limb rest poses differ legitimately (the ninja rests near a T-pose) while spine, neck and head keep the reference pose.",
    "root_scale_finding": "Compiled skeletons have a 100x ancestor scale above the pelvis with bone offsets in metres. The retargeter wrote the pelvis translation in centimetres into that space and emitted unit-scale tracks for the scaled ancestors, which at playback shrank each character to about 2 cm. setup_gallery_playable.py measures the factor, omits IK ops, rescales the pelvis track by 0.01 over 228 keys, strips the ancestor tracks, and composes each pose from the animation data to check it."
